1
00:00:10,877 --> 00:00:13,413
<i>The world is full of coincidences.</i>

2
00:00:14,414 --> 00:00:15,682
<i>Twenty-five years ago,</i>

3
00:00:16,783 --> 00:00:18,785
<i>I had a fateful encounter with Mariko.</i>

4
00:00:20,553 --> 00:00:21,388
<i>However…</i>

5
00:00:22,322 --> 00:00:24,124
<i>there are plenty of people</i>

6
00:00:25,158 --> 00:00:27,527
<i>who approach Mariko those who envy her.</i>

7
00:00:28,028 --> 00:00:30,730
<i>I don't want my daughter</i>
<i>to hear about this.</i>

8
00:00:31,297 --> 00:00:33,466
<i>I must do what I need to.</i>

9
00:00:33,967 --> 00:00:37,437
<i>Yukimura is suspected in Tateiwa's case.</i>

10
00:00:40,540 --> 00:00:42,742
It wasn't on camera, was it?

11
00:00:44,144 --> 00:00:45,912
The part where I killed Tateiwa.

12
00:00:46,913 --> 00:00:48,948
<i>Because I'm the one by Mariko's side…</i>

13
00:00:50,150 --> 00:00:51,117
<i>protecting her.</i>

14
00:00:53,686 --> 00:00:55,989
CRIME PREVENTION

15
00:00:56,056 --> 00:00:58,358
TRAFFIC SAFETY

16
00:01:00,593 --> 00:01:02,829
Somebody! Somebody, help!

17
00:01:03,797 --> 00:01:05,665
Somebody! Somebody! Let me go!

18
00:01:06,533 --> 00:01:09,035
Help me! Let me go!

19
00:01:12,572 --> 00:01:14,107
Somebody!

20
00:01:17,077 --> 00:01:19,746
<i>Mariko! I have to save Mariko…</i>

21
00:01:20,313 --> 00:01:21,281
<i>Mariko!</i>

22
00:01:37,130 --> 00:01:40,500
<i>Recently, I've been having</i>
<i>the same dream over and over.</i>

23
00:01:41,434 --> 00:01:43,903
<i>It's a dream about Mariko</i>
<i>almost being kidnapped</i>

24
00:01:43,970 --> 00:01:45,572
<i>25 years ago.</i>

25
00:01:47,807 --> 00:01:50,376
<i>The me in the dream couldn't make a sound,</i>

26
00:01:50,877 --> 00:01:52,612
<i>and I couldn't save Mariko.</i>

27
00:01:53,947 --> 00:01:55,815
<i>No, that's not it.</i>

28
00:01:56,916 --> 00:01:59,285
<i>I couldn't save Mariko in the dream</i>

29
00:01:59,953 --> 00:02:02,822
<i>because I've always just been a bystander.</i>

30
00:02:29,749 --> 00:02:30,683
<i>It's okay.</i>

31
00:02:31,518 --> 00:02:34,053
<i>In reality, seven-year-old me</i>
<i>did protect her.</i>

32
00:02:39,392 --> 00:02:40,527
<i>And it's a new day.</i>

33
00:02:42,529 --> 00:02:48,768
MAIN TITLE

34
00:03:00,046 --> 00:03:01,181
Good morning.

35
00:03:21,701 --> 00:03:25,939
Come on. How is he always there?

36
00:03:26,005 --> 00:03:27,373
Don't scare me like that!

37
00:03:30,143 --> 00:03:31,010
Why?

38
00:03:31,844 --> 00:03:34,581
Why should I be startled? Me?

39
00:03:50,396 --> 00:03:53,566
Manager, Chitose Chemical
delivered the new sample

40
00:03:53,633 --> 00:03:55,735
based on the feedback from last time.

41
00:03:55,802 --> 00:03:57,704
Just leave it there.
I will review it later.

42
00:04:02,408 --> 00:04:05,144
She is in a terrible mood today.

43
00:04:05,211 --> 00:04:07,880
Something bad must have happened.

44
00:04:28,735 --> 00:04:30,136
She flat out…

45
00:04:32,138 --> 00:04:33,573
hates me.

46
00:04:34,207 --> 00:04:37,543
Whenever she sees your face,
she just walks away disgustedly?

47
00:04:41,547 --> 00:04:45,318
I brazenly intervened in Mariko's
personal life. Now she hates me.

48
00:04:46,719 --> 00:04:48,755
What happened, really?

49
00:04:51,391 --> 00:04:53,793
It's to do with her private life.
I can't tell you.

50
00:04:55,828 --> 00:04:56,796
<i>You</i> are saying that?

51
00:04:59,465 --> 00:05:01,934
Tomoya, excuse me, it won't start…

52
00:05:02,001 --> 00:05:04,570
Ah, okay, okay. Time to focus.

53
00:05:05,305 --> 00:05:06,639
Okay, okay, all right.

54
00:05:07,874 --> 00:05:09,842
Ah, I'm starving.

55
00:05:09,909 --> 00:05:12,178
I missed breakfast this morning.

56
00:05:16,049 --> 00:05:19,319
-Izumi, let's go to a different place.
-What, why?

57
00:05:19,385 --> 00:05:20,386
Well, you know,

58
00:05:20,453 --> 00:05:22,922
-it's crowded in here!
-No, it's empty.

59
00:05:22,989 --> 00:05:25,591
-Just come on! Let's go!
-Why?

60
00:05:26,125 --> 00:05:27,460
I was just leaving.

61
00:05:28,061 --> 00:05:29,529
Yukimura…

62
00:05:29,595 --> 00:05:31,297
-Tap, please.
-Go ahead.

63
00:05:33,099 --> 00:05:35,702
-Thank you.
-Thank you very much. Excuse me.

64
00:05:45,812 --> 00:05:46,946
Did he leave?

65
00:05:54,387 --> 00:05:56,889
Really, it's nothing.

66
00:06:00,793 --> 00:06:01,694
It's just…

67
00:06:02,929 --> 00:06:06,399
I showed a really pathetic side
of myself to a coworker,

68
00:06:07,500 --> 00:06:09,535
so it's awkward, to say the least.

69
00:06:09,602 --> 00:06:11,070
A pathetic side?

70
00:06:11,137 --> 00:06:13,706
Oh, well, it's no big deal.

71
00:06:14,941 --> 00:06:16,909
I just revealed
too much of my private life.

72
00:06:16,976 --> 00:06:20,713
You don't show your private life
to just anyone, Mariko.

73
00:06:20,780 --> 00:06:25,218
It makes me wonder
who Yukimura really is to you.

74
00:06:25,284 --> 00:06:26,853
You're exaggerating.

75
00:06:27,453 --> 00:06:31,324
-Yukimura's great though, isn't he?
-What?

76
00:06:31,391 --> 00:06:35,728
I mean, are things going well with
that policeman you met at the matchmaking?

77
00:06:36,262 --> 00:06:37,730
Well, it's not…

78
00:06:37,797 --> 00:06:39,899
Mariko, you went to a matchmaking?
You dating anyone?

79
00:06:39,966 --> 00:06:42,101
Aren't you supposed to be working?

80
00:06:42,168 --> 00:06:44,303
It's fine, it's fine.
We barely have any customers.

81
00:06:45,204 --> 00:06:47,173
-Are you sure it's fine?
-Yes, I'm sure.

82
00:06:47,240 --> 00:06:49,375
So, are you dating that matchmaking guy?

83
00:06:49,442 --> 00:06:51,244
No, I'm not dating him.

84
00:06:52,678 --> 00:06:54,514
I see. Thank goodness.

85
00:06:55,281 --> 00:06:56,115
Thank goodness?

86
00:06:57,950 --> 00:06:59,218
Just talking to myself.

87
00:06:59,952 --> 00:07:02,588
Speaking of which,
I've been meaning to ask.

88
00:07:02,655 --> 00:07:04,857
Mariko, what's your type?

89
00:07:05,758 --> 00:07:07,360
I've never asked her that either.

90
00:07:09,996 --> 00:07:13,299
I haven't fully analyzed it yet, but…

91
00:07:13,366 --> 00:07:14,667
-Analyzed?
-Analyzed?

92
00:07:15,768 --> 00:07:18,171
…an age range within
five years older or younger.

93
00:07:18,237 --> 00:07:20,706
Living in the central
metropolitan area, male.

94
00:07:20,773 --> 00:07:22,508
Occupation doesn't matter,

95
00:07:22,575 --> 00:07:24,577
but it's best if his days off
are the same as mine.

96
00:07:24,644 --> 00:07:28,214
Also, I'm aware that I can be
lacking in communication at times.

97
00:07:28,281 --> 00:07:30,416
While I'll strive to improve on that,

98
00:07:30,950 --> 00:07:33,853
I believe someone talkative, someone

99
00:07:33,920 --> 00:07:36,489
who immediately voices
any questions or doubts, would be ideal.

100
00:07:37,256 --> 00:07:38,090
Yes.

101
00:07:38,825 --> 00:07:40,593
Is that a type?

102
00:07:41,260 --> 00:07:43,996
You sound like you're filling out
a matchmaking requirement sheet.

103
00:07:47,066 --> 00:07:49,869
Why not follow your heart a bit more?

104
00:07:51,804 --> 00:07:52,738
Follow my heart?

105
00:07:54,474 --> 00:07:57,210
When there's a spark in your heart,

106
00:07:57,276 --> 00:07:59,212
you just follow it.

107
00:08:01,514 --> 00:08:05,251
E-Exactly! Well said, Izumi-chan.

108
00:08:05,318 --> 00:08:06,452
Izumi-chan?

109
00:08:06,519 --> 00:08:09,555
I'm quite a bit older than you,
you know? Plus, I've got a kid.

110
00:08:10,523 --> 00:08:12,959
Is this sexual harassment?
Will your husband get mad at me?

111
00:08:30,443 --> 00:08:33,913
By the way, what kind of guys
have you dated in the past?

112
00:08:33,980 --> 00:08:36,716
Guys who seemed like
they weren't bad people.

113
00:08:36,782 --> 00:08:38,851
No wonder it never lasts.

114
00:08:38,918 --> 00:08:40,820
Some people are just like that…

115
00:08:43,723 --> 00:08:44,757
Hello.

116
00:08:45,458 --> 00:08:46,792
Hello.

117
00:08:52,632 --> 00:08:53,699
Oh, Manager…

118
00:08:54,800 --> 00:08:57,003
-Hello.
-Hey there.

119
00:08:57,537 --> 00:08:59,872
Perfect timing, Mariko.
Are you free tonight?

120
00:08:59,939 --> 00:09:01,407
Yes, I am.

121
00:09:01,474 --> 00:09:04,210
I'm meeting with a professor
from Hokuo University. You're joining us.

122
00:09:04,277 --> 00:09:06,112
-Understood.
-Seto, what time?

123
00:09:06,178 --> 00:09:07,547
7:30 p.m.

124
00:09:07,613 --> 00:09:10,816
I'll send you the details shortly.

125
00:09:10,883 --> 00:09:12,451
-All right.
-What about Asai?

126
00:09:14,353 --> 00:09:15,721
He's taking some time off.

127
00:09:16,923 --> 00:09:19,392
Seto will be covering my schedule for now,

128
00:09:19,458 --> 00:09:20,626
so contact him if anything comes up.

129
00:09:21,227 --> 00:09:22,128
For a while?

130
00:09:27,967 --> 00:09:30,069
Did something happen to Asai?

131
00:09:30,603 --> 00:09:32,038
Is he sick or something?

132
00:09:33,005 --> 00:09:33,906
I wonder…

133
00:09:48,621 --> 00:09:50,022
Hey, somebody!

134
00:09:52,458 --> 00:09:54,527
Hey, is anybody there?

135
00:09:56,529 --> 00:09:59,198
I GOT EVERYONE A LOT OF SWEETS
EAT UP! ASAI

136
00:10:08,007 --> 00:10:11,911
<i>There are lots of things in this world</i>
<i>you don't need to know about.</i>

137
00:10:15,715 --> 00:10:20,286
<i>But those who have opened the door,</i>
<i>can't go back.</i>

138
00:10:35,601 --> 00:10:39,639
SECRETARY'S OFFICE

139
00:10:48,247 --> 00:10:49,382
<i>Mariko.</i>

140
00:10:50,016 --> 00:10:52,284
<i>In order to protect you,</i>

141
00:10:52,351 --> 00:10:54,120
<i>I'm doing some pretty questionable things.</i>

142
00:10:55,554 --> 00:10:58,257
<i>If I'm caught,</i>
<i>I can't talk my way out of this.</i>

143
00:10:59,258 --> 00:11:00,826
<i>I may get fired</i>

144
00:11:01,460 --> 00:11:05,364
<i>or even end up in prison…</i>

145
00:11:10,469 --> 00:11:11,837
NOSE

146
00:11:11,904 --> 00:11:14,473
NOSE COSMETICS, LTD.

147
00:11:20,012 --> 00:11:21,981
SERIAL CHILD KIDNAPPER

148
00:11:25,718 --> 00:11:27,153
<i>It was here after all.</i>

149
00:11:28,354 --> 00:11:30,289
<i>The article from 25 years ago.</i>

150
00:11:30,790 --> 00:11:33,059
<i>An article I've never seen,</i>
<i>one not even in my possession.</i>

151
00:11:33,559 --> 00:11:34,393
CONTRADICTS POLICE STATEMENT

152
00:11:34,460 --> 00:11:37,129
<i>Is Asai Mariko's enemy?</i>

153
00:11:37,196 --> 00:11:38,564
<i>Or her ally?</i>

154
00:11:38,631 --> 00:11:39,665
CONNECTION WITH FATHER LEAVES DOUBT
WAS THE KIDNAPPING TRULY RANDOM?

155
00:11:48,641 --> 00:11:51,143
<i>I just need to get Asai</i>

156
00:11:51,877 --> 00:11:53,846
<i>to share his secret with me.</i>

157
00:11:54,346 --> 00:11:55,748
<i>That's all.</i>

158
00:11:56,682 --> 00:11:57,917
<i>That's all I need…</i>

159
00:12:06,926 --> 00:12:08,828
<i>Don't scare me!</i>

160
00:12:08,894 --> 00:12:12,331
<i>Those big eyes, suddenly staring at me,</i>
<i>scare me more than anything else.</i>

161
00:12:22,675 --> 00:12:25,511
<i>My mother used to tell me</i>

162
00:12:27,379 --> 00:12:32,251
<i>that I only looked at what's in front</i>
<i>of me and never thought about the future.</i>

163
00:12:33,619 --> 00:12:35,154
<i>"I'm sorry, Mom."</i>

164
00:12:35,654 --> 00:12:38,824
<i>They say you can't teach</i>
<i>an old dog new tricks.</i>

165
00:12:38,891 --> 00:12:39,992
<i>And it's true.</i>

166
00:12:41,327 --> 00:12:45,064
<i>Even if I die and go to hell someday,</i>

167
00:12:46,332 --> 00:12:48,701
<i>as long as I can avoid</i>
<i>going to prison right now,</i>

168
00:12:49,602 --> 00:12:50,703
<i>that's enough.</i>

169
00:12:52,972 --> 00:12:54,240
GINJIRO NOSE

170
00:12:58,577 --> 00:12:59,945
GINJIRO NOSE

171
00:13:00,012 --> 00:13:00,646
INCORRECT PASSWORD

172
00:13:02,414 --> 00:13:03,516
INCORRECT PASSWORD

173
00:13:05,017 --> 00:13:08,287
<i>There must be 50,000 combinations…</i>

174
00:13:12,158 --> 00:13:13,392
KEIMEI UNIVERSITY, CLASS OF 1989

175
00:13:13,459 --> 00:13:14,627
TO THE FRIENDS AT THE UNIVERSITY
ROWING CLUB, REUNITING AFTER 30 YEARS

176
00:13:28,541 --> 00:13:29,875
HUMAN RESOURCES - BUSINESS RELATIONS

177
00:13:29,942 --> 00:13:31,143
INTERNAL ESTIMATES

178
00:13:33,312 --> 00:13:34,446
EMAIL

179
00:13:39,618 --> 00:13:40,419
GOTO ASAI

180
00:13:40,486 --> 00:13:41,987
GOOD MORNING, THIS IS ASAI

181
00:13:42,054 --> 00:13:43,956
DUE TO MY MOTHER'S POOR HEALTH

182
00:13:44,023 --> 00:13:45,591
I WILL BE TAKING AN EXTENDED LEAVE

183
00:14:23,295 --> 00:14:25,497
Sorry about that.
Thanks for watching the room.

184
00:14:25,564 --> 00:14:27,099
No problem at all.

185
00:14:27,166 --> 00:14:29,068
The front alarm was malfunctioning.

186
00:14:29,668 --> 00:14:31,237
Didn't seem like
anything was wrong, though.

187
00:14:31,303 --> 00:14:33,906
I see. That's a relief.

188
00:14:33,973 --> 00:14:36,909
Let's eat those snacks you brought us.

189
00:14:37,543 --> 00:14:38,444
Thanks as always.

190
00:14:40,312 --> 00:14:42,047
<i>I was lucky.</i>

191
00:14:43,482 --> 00:14:45,050
<i>Close call.</i>

192
00:14:48,520 --> 00:14:51,223
-Thanks a lot.
-Thank you for the meal.

193
00:14:51,290 --> 00:14:53,125
-I look forward to meeting you again.
-Likewise.

194
00:14:58,697 --> 00:15:01,200
Thank you for tonight.
I'll be taking my leave.

195
00:15:01,267 --> 00:15:04,670
Ride with me. I'll drive you home.

196
00:15:04,737 --> 00:15:07,006
-That's fine. Trains are still running.
-Just come.

197
00:15:17,383 --> 00:15:19,018
<i>I have a bad feeling about this.</i>

198
00:15:20,152 --> 00:15:20,986
<i>And</i>

199
00:15:21,520 --> 00:15:26,125
<i>I hope she forgives me, who, idiotically,</i>
<i>realized this bad feeling too late.</i>

200
00:15:55,854 --> 00:16:00,159
From now on, make sure you never
walk around alone late at night.

201
00:16:02,594 --> 00:16:04,096
Shall I get you a chauffeur?

202
00:16:04,763 --> 00:16:05,898
What?

203
00:16:05,965 --> 00:16:07,533
Remember the Tateiwa case?

204
00:16:08,834 --> 00:16:10,102
Be careful.

205
00:16:12,304 --> 00:16:13,138
Okay…

206
00:16:14,573 --> 00:16:17,009
Oh, but I don't need a chauffeur.

207
00:16:20,612 --> 00:16:21,847
I see…

208
00:16:29,121 --> 00:16:29,955
Um…

209
00:16:32,725 --> 00:16:34,860
I'm sorry about the other day.

210
00:16:37,663 --> 00:16:39,431
Mom's ring…

211
00:16:40,265 --> 00:16:42,634
I know Sayuri had it fixed

212
00:16:43,168 --> 00:16:45,237
out of good intentions.

213
00:16:46,839 --> 00:16:48,340
Tell her I said thank you.

214
00:17:02,755 --> 00:17:04,823
A CONTRADICTION IN THE POLICE REPORT

215
00:17:04,890 --> 00:17:06,625
<i>A contradiction in the police report.</i>

216
00:17:08,227 --> 00:17:12,297
<i>Why didn't the police make this fact</i>
<i>public in the first place?</i>

217
00:17:13,599 --> 00:17:15,267
<i>Did the president cover it up?</i>

218
00:17:15,334 --> 00:17:17,069
TORU URAHARA - CROSSLINE PUBLISHING

219
00:17:22,541 --> 00:17:24,476
CROSSLINE PUBLISHING

220
00:17:25,711 --> 00:17:27,646
TORU URAHARA - CROSSLINE PUBLISHING

221
00:17:31,950 --> 00:17:34,486
GOOD MORNING, THIS IS ASAI

222
00:17:35,154 --> 00:17:36,822
SATORU HATANO

223
00:17:39,625 --> 00:17:43,662
<i>Was Asai investigating</i>
<i>something about Hatano?</i>

224
00:17:43,729 --> 00:17:45,097
SATORU HATANO

225
00:17:45,164 --> 00:17:46,632
EXCLUSIVE INTERVIEW - SHOCKING!

226
00:18:10,589 --> 00:18:13,725
I wondered who was snooping around me.

227
00:18:14,793 --> 00:18:17,796
And it turned out to be
the President's henchman.

228
00:18:18,697 --> 00:18:21,600
-Were you told to keep tabs on me?
-No!

229
00:18:21,667 --> 00:18:23,335
The President knows nothing.

230
00:18:23,402 --> 00:18:25,537
-I was acting on my own.
-On your own?

231
00:18:26,171 --> 00:18:27,005
What?

232
00:18:27,539 --> 00:18:30,976
Acting on righteous fury?
What were you planning to do?

233
00:18:34,713 --> 00:18:36,014
Hey!

234
00:18:38,117 --> 00:18:41,587
You told the weekly mags
all sorts of stuff, right?

235
00:18:42,754 --> 00:18:43,822
So?

236
00:18:45,357 --> 00:18:47,159
You wanted to keep me quiet, huh?

237
00:18:49,661 --> 00:18:50,762
Let me out of here.

238
00:18:51,330 --> 00:18:54,299
I won't tell anyone about this.
Let's pretend this never happened.

239
00:18:55,167 --> 00:18:56,602
Hey, I'm begging you!

240
00:18:56,668 --> 00:18:59,071
You were caught once
and suffered for it, right?

241
00:18:59,771 --> 00:19:01,573
Don't commit more crimes!

242
00:19:01,640 --> 00:19:04,376
I was in prison for 25 years.

243
00:19:05,210 --> 00:19:08,280
I want to return the favor.

244
00:19:09,181 --> 00:19:10,015
What on earth

245
00:19:10,949 --> 00:19:12,618
did the President ever do to you?

246
00:19:14,586 --> 00:19:16,455
Let's see.

247
00:19:17,856 --> 00:19:19,625
He did nothing.

248
00:19:20,792 --> 00:19:25,397
He's done nothing, yet he gets
an easy life because his family is rich.

249
00:19:25,931 --> 00:19:27,466
How is that fair?

250
00:19:30,202 --> 00:19:33,772
Ever since we were kids,
I couldn't stand him.

251
00:19:37,976 --> 00:19:40,679
What are you planning to do? Huh?

252
00:19:40,746 --> 00:19:43,282
Is it money? If he gives you
money, you'll be satis--

253
00:19:44,116 --> 00:19:47,653
Well, I wouldn't say no to money.

254
00:19:48,453 --> 00:19:49,354
But

255
00:19:50,155 --> 00:19:53,692
there is something else
that will quell my anger better.

256
00:19:56,728 --> 00:19:59,298
What do you think it is? Huh?

257
00:20:09,074 --> 00:20:12,578
The ratio of carbomer solution
and dimethicone is still high.

258
00:20:12,644 --> 00:20:15,714
It won't create the heavy texture we want.

259
00:20:17,316 --> 00:20:20,452
Let's refine the concept brief a bit more
and resend it to the supplier.

260
00:20:20,519 --> 00:20:21,453
Okay.

261
00:20:21,520 --> 00:20:24,957
Is "high luxury" too vague
of an expression in the first place?

262
00:20:25,490 --> 00:20:27,859
Or am I being too greedy?

263
00:20:27,926 --> 00:20:30,229
Do I have to give up something?

264
00:20:36,235 --> 00:20:38,337
-What?
-Oh, uh,

265
00:20:38,937 --> 00:20:39,838
sorry.

266
00:20:44,643 --> 00:20:47,446
Please forget about what happened
on my birthday.

267
00:20:48,280 --> 00:20:49,381
<i>Something was wrong with me.</i>

268
00:20:51,783 --> 00:20:53,819
I don't remember anything.

269
00:20:56,922 --> 00:20:58,657
Good then.

270
00:21:03,829 --> 00:21:07,633
Yesterday, I actually had
a normal conversation with my father.

271
00:21:08,533 --> 00:21:12,738
He's right. It's useless
to keep acting stubborn at my age.

272
00:21:15,340 --> 00:21:17,075
You really are kind, Mariko.

273
00:21:18,577 --> 00:21:20,245
I think you're the only one
who thinks that.

274
00:21:20,312 --> 00:21:22,314
If so, everyone else must be blind.

275
00:21:29,221 --> 00:21:30,756
All right then, handle the brief.

276
00:21:30,822 --> 00:21:33,058
-Understood.
-Thank you.

277
00:21:53,945 --> 00:21:54,980
So?

278
00:21:55,047 --> 00:21:59,084
Since when have you
liked Mariko, Yukimura?

279
00:21:59,651 --> 00:22:00,519
What?

280
00:22:01,186 --> 00:22:03,622
-I don't--
-You're so easy to read.

281
00:22:05,057 --> 00:22:07,559
I don't think Mariko has realized it yet.

282
00:22:08,093 --> 00:22:11,496
She's quite dense.

283
00:22:14,966 --> 00:22:17,803
If you don't say it out loud,

284
00:22:18,337 --> 00:22:20,472
I think she'll go
her entire life without knowing.

285
00:22:42,694 --> 00:22:45,197
PRIVATE INVESTIGATOR

286
00:22:45,864 --> 00:22:47,165
I'm sorry,

287
00:22:47,232 --> 00:22:50,502
but it'd be a breach of confidentiality
to give you client information.

288
00:22:50,569 --> 00:22:53,205
But Tateiwa was telling me about it

289
00:22:53,271 --> 00:22:56,808
before he passed away.

290
00:22:56,875 --> 00:22:59,878
He said if anything happened to him,
I must come here for information.

291
00:23:01,646 --> 00:23:03,882
I mean, if he hadn't told me that,

292
00:23:03,949 --> 00:23:07,552
then how would I know to come here?

293
00:23:08,887 --> 00:23:10,088
Excuse me for asking,

294
00:23:10,856 --> 00:23:13,125
but what was your relationship
with Tateiwa?

295
00:23:13,825 --> 00:23:15,360
If I tell you,
will you give me information?

296
00:23:16,194 --> 00:23:17,896
I can't. No way.

297
00:23:17,963 --> 00:23:19,164
Sorry.

298
00:23:32,344 --> 00:23:34,579
No! I can't.

299
00:23:34,646 --> 00:23:39,518
This is just my gratitude
for our meeting today.

300
00:23:40,352 --> 00:23:41,653
Nothing else.

301
00:23:47,125 --> 00:23:48,160
What?

302
00:23:52,197 --> 00:23:54,566
I meant to make a phone call.

303
00:23:54,633 --> 00:23:56,968
That's right. Excuse me for a moment.

304
00:23:57,469 --> 00:23:59,404
Let's see…

305
00:24:01,706 --> 00:24:03,341
Excuse me for a moment.

306
00:24:04,810 --> 00:24:07,813
Ah, hello? It's me, it's me.

307
00:24:11,550 --> 00:24:13,151
‎INVESTIGATION REPORT

308
00:24:18,523 --> 00:24:19,591
<i>A love motel room?</i>

309
00:24:19,658 --> 00:24:21,259
Definitely.

310
00:24:22,427 --> 00:24:24,229
I got a call from his wife this afternoon.

311
00:24:24,296 --> 00:24:25,864
She was putting his affairs in order,

312
00:24:25,931 --> 00:24:29,201
and it turns out Tateiwa was renting
a room his family knew nothing about.

313
00:24:30,402 --> 00:24:33,271
It was a plain, ordinary room, but…

314
00:24:33,338 --> 00:24:36,107
It's got to do with his womanizing.

315
00:24:36,842 --> 00:24:40,378
-Did anything turn up in the room?
-No, nothing.

316
00:24:40,445 --> 00:24:42,547
It was unnaturally empty.

317
00:24:42,614 --> 00:24:45,550
There was no data left
on his laptop either.

318
00:24:47,486 --> 00:24:51,823
Did someone who knew about
this room's existence take everything?

319
00:24:52,858 --> 00:24:54,192
I would say his mistress.

320
00:24:59,164 --> 00:25:03,335
According to the autopsy results,
among the three stab wounds,

321
00:25:03,401 --> 00:25:06,204
the one that became the fatal blow
is this chest wound, right?

322
00:25:07,472 --> 00:25:09,307
-Yes.
-And

323
00:25:09,374 --> 00:25:15,380
that fatal chest wound
was likely the very first strike.

324
00:25:17,082 --> 00:25:21,386
Reaching the heart from between
the ribs in the left chest…

325
00:25:22,487 --> 00:25:25,524
To inflict a wound of that depth…

326
00:25:27,192 --> 00:25:28,860
So does that mean the suspect is a man?

327
00:25:29,661 --> 00:25:31,863
Wouldn't you say
that's a strong possibility?

328
00:25:32,397 --> 00:25:34,666
In the end, the most suspicious one

329
00:25:35,200 --> 00:25:37,802
is that man caught on the security camera

330
00:25:38,370 --> 00:25:39,404
near the crime scene.

331
00:25:41,640 --> 00:25:43,441
Sota Yukimura.

332
00:25:47,546 --> 00:25:49,581
But the murder weapon hasn't been found,

333
00:25:49,648 --> 00:25:52,150
and the motive isn't really clear.

334
00:25:52,217 --> 00:25:53,251
SOTA YUKIMURA

335
00:26:02,427 --> 00:26:03,395
Here you go.

336
00:26:03,895 --> 00:26:05,130
Thank you.

337
00:26:06,898 --> 00:26:07,766
Enjoy.

338
00:26:12,170 --> 00:26:13,905
Apologies for bothering you at work.

339
00:26:14,439 --> 00:26:15,340
It's okay.

340
00:26:17,676 --> 00:26:19,110
It's a lovely cafe.

341
00:26:19,778 --> 00:26:21,146
Do you come here often?

342
00:26:21,680 --> 00:26:25,283
Yes, it's close to the company,
and I like the atmosphere.

343
00:26:28,954 --> 00:26:30,822
It's not good to mix business
with private affairs,

344
00:26:31,356 --> 00:26:33,892
so let me state this up front.

345
00:26:35,160 --> 00:26:37,963
Today, we'll talk about work.

346
00:26:39,497 --> 00:26:40,498
Okay.

347
00:26:40,565 --> 00:26:42,334
I heard Souta Yukimura

348
00:26:42,901 --> 00:26:46,504
was transferred to your department
very recently.

349
00:26:48,239 --> 00:26:49,107
Yes.

350
00:26:49,774 --> 00:26:51,109
Is there an issue with that?

351
00:26:51,176 --> 00:26:52,711
It's nothing big.

352
00:26:53,278 --> 00:26:54,112
I just heard

353
00:26:55,013 --> 00:26:57,115
you selected him.

354
00:27:00,518 --> 00:27:03,955
Were you close prior to that?

355
00:27:05,357 --> 00:27:06,191
No.

356
00:27:06,891 --> 00:27:09,794
Even though we're at the same company,
we had no interaction,

357
00:27:10,328 --> 00:27:11,930
so I didn't know him at all.

358
00:27:13,131 --> 00:27:14,766
Then why him?

359
00:27:16,735 --> 00:27:20,438
One time, we had a brief chance to talk,

360
00:27:20,505 --> 00:27:23,341
and I thought he was very capable.

361
00:27:23,908 --> 00:27:24,743
I see.

362
00:27:26,711 --> 00:27:29,914
What's Yukimura usually like?

363
00:27:31,950 --> 00:27:32,951
Um,

364
00:27:33,618 --> 00:27:36,454
does this have to do with the case?

365
00:27:37,489 --> 00:27:38,390
I'm sorry.

366
00:27:38,990 --> 00:27:41,426
-We're investigating from all angles.
-So,

367
00:27:41,493 --> 00:27:43,028
you really do suspect Yukimura?

368
00:27:47,298 --> 00:27:48,600
I'm sorry.

369
00:27:48,667 --> 00:27:50,168
You can't answer that, right?

370
00:27:51,302 --> 00:27:52,203
No.

371
00:27:52,804 --> 00:27:55,040
I've never been involved
with a criminal case before.

372
00:27:55,974 --> 00:27:58,276
I mean, it's not exactly normal.

373
00:27:59,678 --> 00:28:02,681
So, honestly, I still can't believe it.

374
00:28:03,748 --> 00:28:04,849
Yes.

375
00:28:05,950 --> 00:28:06,851
But

376
00:28:08,286 --> 00:28:10,622
I really think Yukimura is different.

377
00:28:12,457 --> 00:28:14,325
He's… How do I put it?

378
00:28:15,226 --> 00:28:18,963
He's someone who always worries
about others rather than himself.

379
00:28:19,564 --> 00:28:21,533
Someone who seems like
he couldn't even kill a bug.

380
00:28:22,600 --> 00:28:25,270
He probably came under suspicion

381
00:28:25,336 --> 00:28:27,305
because of my relationship with Tateiwa,

382
00:28:27,372 --> 00:28:29,007
but he really is innocent.

383
00:28:33,812 --> 00:28:37,115
I understand what you're saying.

384
00:28:45,490 --> 00:28:46,491
Mariko.

385
00:28:47,292 --> 00:28:48,993
Here you go.

386
00:28:50,428 --> 00:28:51,863
Thank you very much.

387
00:28:52,997 --> 00:28:54,499
Was that the matchmaking guy?

388
00:28:56,434 --> 00:29:00,071
So he was! Are you going to date him?

389
00:29:01,673 --> 00:29:03,842
I think he seems like a nice person, but…

390
00:29:07,812 --> 00:29:10,582
Don't you feel like you and I are similar?

391
00:29:12,083 --> 00:29:13,918
I've never felt
a spark with anyone either.

392
00:29:15,987 --> 00:29:18,690
What were you like
back in your student days?

393
00:29:18,757 --> 00:29:20,158
Any bittersweet memories?

394
00:29:21,693 --> 00:29:23,595
Even I have that much…

395
00:29:25,363 --> 00:29:26,765
In middle school,

396
00:29:27,532 --> 00:29:29,200
<i>I was asked on a date</i>
<i>to a summer festival.</i>

397
00:29:30,769 --> 00:29:33,238
<i>It was my first time going out with a boy,</i>

398
00:29:33,304 --> 00:29:36,307
<i>so I was nervous</i>
<i>and couldn't talk much at all.</i>

399
00:29:37,175 --> 00:29:39,744
Cute. Classic story.

400
00:29:40,512 --> 00:29:41,479
But

401
00:29:41,546 --> 00:29:45,683
to him, it probably looked like
I wasn't having any fun at all.

402
00:29:47,552 --> 00:29:49,754
So he left halfway through and went home.

403
00:29:50,288 --> 00:29:51,189
What? He left you?

404
00:29:52,023 --> 00:29:54,726
-I guess…
-Wow, that guy sucks.

405
00:29:54,793 --> 00:29:57,128
No, it was 100% my fault.

406
00:29:57,195 --> 00:29:59,564
I was expressionless.
You couldn't tell what I was thinking.

407
00:29:59,631 --> 00:30:01,299
He must be scared.

408
00:30:02,467 --> 00:30:03,401
So you are aware of it.

409
00:30:04,736 --> 00:30:05,603
I guess so.

410
00:30:05,670 --> 00:30:07,806
But did you feel a spark with that boy?

411
00:30:08,740 --> 00:30:11,476
No, I didn't.

412
00:30:11,543 --> 00:30:13,578
The heck, so you never had anyone!

413
00:30:15,680 --> 00:30:18,116
Well, forget it! Enough about me.

414
00:30:24,689 --> 00:30:27,725
I envy it, you know.

415
00:30:29,928 --> 00:30:31,563
It doesn't matter if it works out or not.

416
00:30:31,629 --> 00:30:33,898
It's incredible just to have someone.

417
00:30:36,134 --> 00:30:39,070
That guy too,
he's liked the same girl for a long time.

418
00:30:40,238 --> 00:30:43,341
How someone can keep thinking
of one person for so many years

419
00:30:43,408 --> 00:30:45,243
is a mystery to me.

420
00:30:47,145 --> 00:30:48,847
That's just the kind of guy Sota is.

421
00:31:06,731 --> 00:31:08,299
-Hello.
-Hello.

422
00:31:18,142 --> 00:31:19,143
Here you go.

423
00:31:20,311 --> 00:31:21,145
It's fine.

424
00:31:21,813 --> 00:31:24,782
You don't need to do that.
It's not part of your job.

425
00:31:26,251 --> 00:31:27,218
I'm sorry.

426
00:31:38,229 --> 00:31:40,865
She didn't need to say it so harshly.

427
00:31:42,000 --> 00:31:45,570
But honestly, I thought
it was a bit calculated too.

428
00:31:47,071 --> 00:31:50,074
Serving coffee to get liked
by the boss, you know?

429
00:31:51,409 --> 00:31:54,312
That's not what I was trying to do.

430
00:31:54,379 --> 00:31:58,950
Mariko seriously hates
being given special treatment like that.

431
00:32:01,953 --> 00:32:02,787
<i>Mariko.</i>

432
00:32:03,955 --> 00:32:07,625
<i>Have you been thinking of me</i>
<i>as a calculating person,</i>

433
00:32:07,692 --> 00:32:11,129
<i>trying to win favor</i>
<i>with the boss, ever since then?</i>

434
00:32:16,868 --> 00:32:20,238
-Good work today, everyone. Goodbye.
-Bye.

435
00:32:23,875 --> 00:32:26,377
<i>Was I wrong all along?</i>

436
00:32:43,061 --> 00:32:47,031
<i>Even if Mariko is starting to hate me,</i>

437
00:32:48,633 --> 00:32:50,735
<i>there are still things I must do.</i>

438
00:33:01,479 --> 00:33:03,247
Did I say something I shouldn't have?

439
00:33:04,515 --> 00:33:05,416
What was that?

440
00:33:05,483 --> 00:33:07,452
Oh, nothing.

441
00:33:07,518 --> 00:33:10,321
You certainly do need a man
to help with this, huh?

442
00:33:10,388 --> 00:33:11,289
-Right?
-Yes.

443
00:33:11,356 --> 00:33:13,458
Delivery fees are so high!

444
00:33:13,524 --> 00:33:16,828
-I ran into you at the perfect time.
-No problem.

445
00:33:16,894 --> 00:33:20,131
Kinda feels like a park date, right?

446
00:33:20,732 --> 00:33:24,602
-It's exciting, like we're school kids.
-Sara! We're going home!

447
00:33:24,669 --> 00:33:27,305
What? I don't want to go home yet!

448
00:33:27,372 --> 00:33:30,108
What? I don't want to go home yet!

449
00:33:30,174 --> 00:33:32,477
Hey, that's enough.

450
00:33:32,543 --> 00:33:35,046
-I've got to make dinner.
-Cheapskate!

451
00:33:36,881 --> 00:33:40,284
Okay, if you can take the ball
from me now, you win.

452
00:33:40,351 --> 00:33:41,986
Okay, let's go.

453
00:33:47,191 --> 00:33:48,226
Got it?

454
00:33:49,660 --> 00:33:50,528
Can you reach it?

455
00:33:54,665 --> 00:33:55,967
Not bad.

456
00:34:02,707 --> 00:34:04,609
This was sent to my husband?

457
00:34:04,675 --> 00:34:07,812
Yes. It seems it was sent to him
on the exact day the incident occurred.

458
00:34:08,846 --> 00:34:10,014
Okay.

459
00:34:11,015 --> 00:34:14,352
If you get any more information,
report back to me immediately.

460
00:34:14,419 --> 00:34:15,720
Understood.

461
00:34:36,074 --> 00:34:38,509
TV COMMERCIAL

462
00:34:40,578 --> 00:34:41,913
SHINAGAWA STREET MALE STABBING VICTIM

463
00:34:41,979 --> 00:34:43,147
WAS A NOSE COSMETICS EXECUTIVE!

464
00:34:43,214 --> 00:34:44,649
RUMORS ABOUT THE COMPANY'S SHADY DEALINGS

465
00:34:44,715 --> 00:34:48,052
So people finally found out…

466
00:34:48,119 --> 00:34:50,321
Since major media isn't reporting
the details,

467
00:34:50,388 --> 00:34:52,690
rumors are running wild online

468
00:34:52,757 --> 00:34:54,258
about Nose Cosmetics's shady side.

469
00:34:54,325 --> 00:34:55,393
THE AMBITION OF AN EXECUTIVE

470
00:34:55,460 --> 00:34:58,463
Well, it can't be helped.
The way it all looks…

471
00:34:58,963 --> 00:35:02,967
It sounds like
Mariko will be suspected, right?

472
00:35:10,108 --> 00:35:10,942
Everyone.

473
00:35:15,847 --> 00:35:18,616
I'm changing my schedule today
and going out.

474
00:35:19,350 --> 00:35:22,787
I think the clients
have seen this article too,

475
00:35:22,854 --> 00:35:24,021
so I'll go explain in person.

476
00:35:27,358 --> 00:35:29,861
Um, I'll accompany you.

477
00:35:44,408 --> 00:35:48,012
I'm really sorry about this.

478
00:35:55,887 --> 00:35:58,656
I'm glad everyone was understanding.

479
00:36:02,994 --> 00:36:05,763
Did you follow me, thinking
I was going to get yelled at?

480
00:36:05,830 --> 00:36:06,731
No.

481
00:36:07,398 --> 00:36:08,733
It wasn't like that.

482
00:36:22,680 --> 00:36:24,515
Oh, I'm sorry. I'm sorry.

483
00:36:25,917 --> 00:36:27,185
No, it's fine.

484
00:36:36,494 --> 00:36:38,896
I'm sorry. I'm a bit thirsty.

485
00:36:38,963 --> 00:36:40,064
Can we take a break?

486
00:36:40,631 --> 00:36:42,133
-Oh, sure…
-Sorry.

487
00:37:04,021 --> 00:37:05,656
Which one do you want?

488
00:37:05,723 --> 00:37:07,792
You bought them. You decide.

489
00:37:07,858 --> 00:37:09,026
It's fine.

490
00:37:10,228 --> 00:37:11,229
This one, then.

491
00:37:20,471 --> 00:37:21,339
Also…

492
00:37:22,006 --> 00:37:23,040
Here.

493
00:37:24,275 --> 00:37:25,476
Right there…

494
00:37:27,845 --> 00:37:29,847
What? That's scary. You're too sharp-eyed.

495
00:37:31,415 --> 00:37:33,818
Sorry, that was creepy, right?

496
00:37:35,152 --> 00:37:37,688
No, no, I didn't mean it like that.

497
00:37:39,457 --> 00:37:40,358
Thank you.

498
00:37:51,235 --> 00:37:53,504
-What should we do?
-Hmm, what should we do?

499
00:37:53,571 --> 00:37:55,673
-How about target practice?
-Let's get yakisoba.

500
00:37:55,740 --> 00:37:57,308
-Yes!
-I want yakisoba too.

501
00:37:57,375 --> 00:37:58,909
-Me too!
-Yeah!

502
00:37:58,976 --> 00:38:00,311
I'm starving!

503
00:38:02,647 --> 00:38:04,048
What kind of feeling is it?

504
00:38:06,984 --> 00:38:09,153
You've liked the same person
for a long time, right?

505
00:38:18,062 --> 00:38:20,064
Your friend at the cafe mentioned it.

506
00:38:21,932 --> 00:38:22,933
Tomoya…

507
00:38:25,870 --> 00:38:27,838
What makes you like that person so much?

508
00:38:36,981 --> 00:38:38,649
You probably don't want
to talk about this at work.

509
00:38:38,716 --> 00:38:40,718
I'm sorry, that was impolite.

510
00:38:53,831 --> 00:38:56,801
Her sense of justice, I suppose…

511
00:39:02,340 --> 00:39:06,944
She walks straight down
the path she chose…

512
00:39:09,747 --> 00:39:11,649
and works so hard for it

513
00:39:14,485 --> 00:39:16,554
Even though she stands out so much,

514
00:39:18,556 --> 00:39:21,959
she's not someone who wants to stand out.

515
00:39:27,531 --> 00:39:30,868
When given special treatment,
she makes a sour face…

516
00:39:33,704 --> 00:39:35,840
She's mature, pure-hearted,

517
00:39:37,541 --> 00:39:40,911
and always worrying about stuff.

518
00:39:42,613 --> 00:39:46,817
But she desperately tries
to live without relying on anyone.

519
00:39:49,053 --> 00:39:52,890
She's kind to people, things, everything.

520
00:39:53,858 --> 00:39:55,426
She doesn't lie.

521
00:39:56,927 --> 00:39:59,397
Anyway, she's cool.

522
00:40:08,072 --> 00:40:09,640
She's my hero.

523
00:40:15,312 --> 00:40:18,215
Well, I guess it should be heroine, huh?

524
00:40:23,053 --> 00:40:24,155
Let's go.

525
00:40:29,160 --> 00:40:31,262
I'm sorry. Thank you.

526
00:40:34,732 --> 00:40:35,699
Here.

527
00:40:39,403 --> 00:40:40,604
Sorry.

528
00:40:44,909 --> 00:40:45,776
Here.

529
00:40:46,410 --> 00:40:47,711
I love that character.

530
00:40:47,778 --> 00:40:49,513
KOGEBAN

531
00:40:54,385 --> 00:40:56,554
It was popular back when
I was in middle school.

532
00:40:57,354 --> 00:41:00,057
Once I like something,
I tend to stay attached to it forever.

533
00:41:01,859 --> 00:41:05,129
I still use it. Childish, right?

534
00:41:23,781 --> 00:41:26,083
FESTIVAL

535
00:41:30,287 --> 00:41:33,357
We still have time
until the fireworks. Are you hungry?

536
00:41:33,424 --> 00:41:35,593
-How about some takoyaki?
-Anything's fine.

537
00:41:36,093 --> 00:41:37,895
Hey, Hiroto!

538
00:41:38,462 --> 00:41:40,464
Hiroto, come hang out with us!

539
00:41:40,531 --> 00:41:42,633
Idiot, he's on a date!

540
00:41:42,700 --> 00:41:44,902
-Oh, okay.
-Let's go.

541
00:41:46,036 --> 00:41:46,971
I'm going with them.

542
00:41:48,572 --> 00:41:49,440
Hey!

543
00:41:49,507 --> 00:41:50,474
Hey!

544
00:41:50,541 --> 00:41:52,109
-Let's go!
-What, seriously?

545
00:41:52,176 --> 00:41:53,544
-It's fine, it's fine, let's go!
-What?

546
00:42:04,121 --> 00:42:05,022
Sorry!

547
00:42:08,392 --> 00:42:11,328
FESTIVAL

548
00:42:45,863 --> 00:42:47,298
<i>August 8th.</i>

549
00:42:48,399 --> 00:42:50,067
<i>Today was the summer festival.</i>

550
00:42:51,869 --> 00:42:55,472
<i>Mariko was asked out</i>
<i>on a date by a boy in our class.</i>

551
00:42:57,575 --> 00:42:58,576
<i>To be honest,</i>

552
00:42:59,343 --> 00:43:01,045
<i>my chest felt tight.</i>

553
00:43:02,713 --> 00:43:05,149
<i>Even though I decided to watch over her</i>

554
00:43:06,216 --> 00:43:08,752
<i>and thought that I just</i>
<i>wanted her to be happy…</i>

555
00:43:11,055 --> 00:43:13,190
<i>If he can't see Mariko's charm,</i>

556
00:43:13,757 --> 00:43:14,892
<i>he's got no sense at all.</i>

557
00:43:16,994 --> 00:43:20,030
<i>Mariko, I don't want you to get hurt…</i>

558
00:43:29,974 --> 00:43:30,874
Sakura!

559
00:43:30,941 --> 00:43:31,875
Sakura!

560
00:43:33,310 --> 00:43:34,878
We found DNA from someone

561
00:43:34,945 --> 00:43:37,014
other than the victim
at Tateiwa's murder scene.

562
00:43:37,815 --> 00:43:38,882
What?

563
00:43:38,949 --> 00:43:41,952
There's no match in the police database.

564
00:43:42,586 --> 00:43:43,954
So, in other words…

565
00:43:47,591 --> 00:43:50,594
It's someone with no prior record…

566
00:44:10,180 --> 00:44:12,483
THE STABBING OF AN EXECUTIVE IN SHINAGAWA

567
00:44:13,183 --> 00:44:14,051
I knew it.

568
00:44:15,452 --> 00:44:17,655
It was your doing.

569
00:44:20,124 --> 00:44:23,694
It'd be troublesome for me if Mariko
gained any more power, wouldn't it?

570
00:44:26,764 --> 00:44:29,199
You really are incredible.

571
00:44:29,266 --> 00:44:30,634
My investigation was correct.

572
00:44:31,201 --> 00:44:33,871
I looked into you too, you know.

573
00:44:35,005 --> 00:44:38,108
Your background is very interesting.

574
00:44:39,743 --> 00:44:40,978
What are you

575
00:44:42,146 --> 00:44:43,647
to Mariko?

576
00:45:08,038 --> 00:45:08,972
Subtitle translation by:
